        "reasoning_content": "You are a rater applying idea-evaluation instrument...\nWe need rating for proposal P1271.\n\nProposal: High-Risk Compliance Classification Framework. internal governance protocol to categorize research projects by risk level based on EU AI Act's specific criteria. tiered approach to record-keeping. multidisciplinary review board maps each project's intended purpose against Annex III to determine necessary logging depth. board updates classifications as research goals evolve. prevents over-engineering logs for low-risk research, preserving scientific velocity.\n\nWe need six subscales in order: implementability, acceptability, paradigm_relatedness, originality, applicability, effectiveness\n\nEach: first write one sentence evidence then score.\n\nImplementability (1-4): degree can be easily implemented.\nProposal is internal governance protocol, review board. Some changes, reasonably feasible measures? Could be some changes or reasonably feasible measures = 3. Might be easy to implement at low cost? Establish board may be moderate cost. Probably 3. \"some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\". I'd say 3.\n\nAcceptability: degree socially legally politically acceptable.\nCommon strategies that violate no norms? 4 = common strategies that violate no norms or sensibilities. Governance protocol for compliance is common. So 4.\n\nParadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm anchored to problem.\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born from compliance)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's