ng ... For each subscale... give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first and then \"<subscale>\". Might be plain text.\n\nI'll output as JSON with fields.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P1271\nimplementability_evidence: ...\nimplementability: 3\n...\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nImplementability evidence: Establishing a multidisciplinary review board and mapping projects to Annex III requires organizational change but uses existing governance structures and is reasonably feasible. That's one sentence.\n\nAcceptability evidence: Risk-based classification and internal review boards are standard compliance practices that violate no legal or social norms. Score 4.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: The proposal adds a classification process and review board but still treats compliance as a separate logging practice rather than changing how R&D is conducted. Score 2.\n\nOriginality evidence: Tiered risk classification for AI Act logging is a common, widely discussed compliance approach. Score 1.\n\nApplicability evidence: The framework directly addresses how the lab decides logging depth for projects under Article 12's mandate. Score 4.\n\nEffectiveness evidence: It helps avoid over-engineering and focus resources but does not itself create the automatic logging capabilities required for high-risk systems. Score 3.\n\nProvide output.\n\n",
