        "reasoning_content": "You are a rater applying idea-evaluation instrument...\n\nWe need rate proposal P2591.\n\nProposal: Log Integrity and Traceability Validation Suite. testing framework simulates system failures and edge cases to verify if automatic logs accurately capture required risk-related events. develop suite adversarial test cases trigger specific risk flags ensure logging mechanisms functioning as intended before deployment. ensures technical viability and prevents lab from deploying high-risk systems with silent logging failures.\n\nWe need six subscales in order: implementability, acceptability, paradigm_relatedness, originality, applicability, effectiveness\n\nEach: one sentence evidence then score.\n\nImplementability (1-4): degree can be easily implemented.\nEasy to implement at low cost or non-radical changes =4\nsome changes reasonably feasible =3\nsignificant change expensive difficult but not impossible=2\ntotally infeasible=1\n\nProposal is testing framework. Seems some changes, reasonably feasible measures. Developing test suite is engineering work. Likely 3? Could be 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Might be easy? Requires developing adversarial test cases. Probably some changes. I'd say 3.\n\nAcceptability: degree socially legally politically acceptable.\n4=common strategies violate no norms\n3=somewhat uncommon unusual strategies do not offend sensibilities\n2=offends somewhat but not totally unacceptable\n1=radically violates\n\nTesting logs for compliance is common, acceptable. 4 = common strategies that violate no norms. Could be 3? I'd say 4.\n\nParadigm_relatedness: degree preserves or modifies paradigm anchored to problem.\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born