date? Transform logs into interpretability framework still requires logs. It provides logging capability and adds value. Reasonable will solve stated problem? Might be partial? It meets logging requirement plus adapt R&D. Could be 4. If you could do it, it would solve main problem of meeting mandate and adapting R&D. Probably 3? Hmm.\n\nThe proposal is about using logs for interpretability, not just compliance. Effectiveness at meeting logging mandate: capturing latent state activations may exceed requirement but still meets. Might be effective.\n\nI think effectiveness = 3? It contributes to solution: it helps meet mandate but maybe over-engineered? Could be 4.\n\nGiven anchored: reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability (if you could do it, it would solve main problem). If you could build API capturing latent activations, you'd have logs and adapt R&D. Seems solves.\n\nLet's give 3 for originality, 3 for paradigm_relatedness, 2 for implementability, 3 for acceptability, 4 for applicability, 4 for effectiveness? Hmm.\n\nCheck consistency: implementability 2 (significant change expensive). Acceptability 3.\n\nProvide output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably need JSON? Probably plain lines.\n\nReturn rating of proposal, echoing its id exactly. For each subscale... give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first then \"<subscale>\".\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P2807\n\noriginality_evidence: ...\noriginality: 3\n\netc.\n\nMake one sentence evidence each.\n\nLet's craft concise sentences.\n\nOriginality evidence: The proposal reframes mandatory logs as an interpretability dataset, which is unusual for compliance responses and shows imagination. Score 3.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: It weaves logging into scientific model analysis, changing the relationship between R&D and compliance obligations rather than treating logs as mere paperwork. Score 3.\n\nImplementability evide