g. 1 = common mundane boring.\nUnified logging framework is common, mundane. So 1? Could be 2 = interesting. Probably common practice. I'd say 1 = common, mundane, boring.\n\nImplementability (1-4): 4 easy low cost non-radical; 3 some changes reasonably feasible; 2 significant change expensive difficult but not impossible; 1 totally infeasible.\nDeveloping middleware library is some changes reasonably feasible. Might be significant change? Engineering teams develop middleware layer... likely some changes, reasonably feasible. So 3.\n\nAcceptability (1-4): 4 common strategies violate no norms; 3 somewhat uncommon... do not offend; etc. This is common. 4 = common strategies that violate no norms or sensibilities. So 4.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4): degree will solve problem. 4 reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard workability. Proposal ensures baseline regulatory compliance across various research streams without requiring each team build own logging architecture. Does it meet Article12? It captures timestamps and system states into immutable searchable ledger. Article requires logs of events relevant for identifying risk, post-market monitoring etc., and specific items for point 1(a) Annex III. Timestamps and system states may be baseline but not necessarily sufficient. Might be partial solution. So effectiveness = 3? Reasonable and will contribute to solution but only partial. Probably 3.\n\nApplicability (1-4): degree clearly applies to stated problem. 4 solves identified problem directly related. Do X to get Y, Y is part of stated problem. Unified logging addresses automatic event recording mandate. So 4.\n\nProvide output.\n\nNeed format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence one sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably JSON? Instruction says return rating... Probably list.\n\nWill output:\n\nid: P2960\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n...\n\nLet's ensure one sentence evidence.\n\nParadigm_related